+## A failed beforeSession
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws reaches the caller as the same rejection it always did, and reaches `onError` with the same session-and-error arguments any other failure in the turn delivers ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws, and still rejects the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L20)).
+- `afterSession` runs for that same throw, after `onError`, with a session no provider call has touched, so a cleanup hook can release what its own `beforeSession` allocated but cannot assume any other part of the turn happened; the hook arguments do not distinguish a session that never started from one that failed mid-turn, and a deployer that needs the distinction records it in its own `beforeSession` ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws, and still rejects the caller](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L20)).
